# Text is normalised by core.autocrlf; these are the formats git must not touch.
*.bin   binary
*.dll   binary
*.lib   binary
*.exp   binary
*.obj   binary
*.pdb   binary
*.sav   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.uasset binary
*.umap  binary
*.pak   binary

# Batch files must keep CRLF in the working tree: cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only .bat
# files in some configurations, and the symptom is a silently skipped block.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# NOTE: mod/native/src/targets.h and mod/doc/vectors.txt are generated, but their
# diffs are deliberately NOT suppressed.  A change to targets.h means the game build
# changed (every RVA is byte-verified against it), and a change to vectors.txt means
# the wire format changed.  Both are things a reviewer must see.
